answers={11:('o2','The cited stack names SLAM mapping, AMCL prebuilt-map localization, Nav2 navigation and YOLO object perception; the alternatives swap those subsystem roles.'),23:('o3','For coordinates p_base, p_odom=T_odom,base p_base, then p_map=T_map,odom p_odom. Substitution yields the ordered product; rightmost map acts first.'),25:('o1','A changed physical camera extrinsic invalidates the stored geometry. Algebraic consistency of a transform tree does not guarantee physical calibration.'),29:('o3','The plane can miss a low obstacle while registered depth observes it. Missing planar evidence is not proof of unoccupied three-dimensional volume.'),31:('o1','Clearance depends on the swept footprint plus margins, not just the point centerline or endpoint. The question labels this an added finite-body interpretation.'),38:('o4','Two hypotheses can remain plausible. Equal likelihood does not force equal posterior without equal priors; a mixture mean can lie in a low-density region.'),48:('o1','The page assigns functional tasks but contains no launch/process graph. The arrows and independent-executable simplification do not establish either one-process-per-box or shared composition.'),54:('o3','Axial Z=.001×1500=1.5m; X=(420−320)×1.5/500=.3m; Y=(240−240)×1.5/500=0. Result(.3,0,1.5)m. Recomputed despite prior old concept-description exposure.'),55:('o2','Different viewpoints give different projection rays. Equal array indices/resizing do not themselves establish correspondence; registration or explicit geometry is required.'),57:('o3','The table separates modeldescription, worldgeometry and virtualmeasurements. It does not substitute navigation algorithms for sensors or assume noisefree poseonly outputs.'),65:('o3','Unchanged command but falling measured speed under load motivates feedback, controller/driver limits and supply checks. This is diagnostic prioritization, not proof of a particular fault.'),66:('o1','The table describes structured/model-based versus sensor-based dynamic-setting emphasis and separately says the robot mixes AI and classical methods. Do not infer impossibility or replacement of all control.'),67:('o1','Actual pixels show the EKF box splits to upperSLAM and lowerLocalisationAMCL. YOLO/costmap and motorbranches are separate.'),68:('o1','Actual order desiredwheelvelocity→PID→PWM→DCmotor→encoder; accompanying text says continual correction. No unprinted feedback-return arrow needs to be invented.'),69:('o1','The black GlobalPlannedPath arrow points to longgreenlefttrace; LocalPlannerPath arrow points to the shorttrace beside redrobot.'),70:('o1','ProcessingNodes has one rightarrow toNavigation and one downwardarrow toMotorController, followedby MobileRobot. There is no Navigation→MotorController arrow drawn.')}
